# What does NOT get uploaded to Cloud Build by `gcloud run deploy --source`.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, gcloud INFERS exclusions from .gitignore.
# That worked, but it meant the only thing keeping .env out of an upload was
# implicit behaviour — too load-bearing for a secret to rely on.
#
# The trade: this file REPLACES that inference, so the list below must be
# complete. Anything not excluded here IS uploaded, even if .gitignore covers
# it. Add to both files when adding something that should stay local.
#
# Note this is NOT a copy of .dockerignore. That one excludes the Dockerfile
# itself; Cloud Build needs it, so it must not be excluded here.

# --- secrets and local state ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.localdata/

# --- reinstalled or regenerated inside the image ---
# node_modules: `npm ci` runs in the build stage.
# bundle.js:    `npm run build:client` runs in the build stage.
**/node_modules/
virtual_space/client/static/bundle.js
**/dist/

# --- local data, never part of a deploy ---
**/data/
**/output/
**/*.jsonl
**/*.log

# --- working material that is not the application ---
# ref/ is third-party (colleagues' syllabi, course handouts) and must not be
# redistributed; user_requirements/ and plan/ are working documents.
ref/
user_requirements/
improvements/
**/docs/improvements/
plan/

# --- repo and OS noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store
